  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Carahsoft Technology has $1.4B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Carahsoft Technology won 1,529 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $941K. Carahsoft Technology saw obligations fall 20.5% year over year. Carahsoft Technology receives the largest share of FY2026 obligations from the Department of Defense, which obligated $695M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $233M and the Department of Homeland Security at $115M. Carahsoft Technology’s top markets are led by Software Publishers, which account for $1B and an additional Software Publishers category at $110M, and Other Computer Related Services at $221M. Carahsoft Technology’s FY2026 total sits below the FY24 and FY25 obligations of $1.8B each, and matches the FY23 obligation of $1.4B. This profile shows concentrated demand in software and IT services and strong buying from defense and health agencies in the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did Carahsoft Technology’s obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Carahsoft Technology’s obligations fell 20.5% year over year. Carahsoft Technology’s FY2026 obligations of $1.4B are smaller than FY24 and FY25 obligations of $1.8B and equal to FY23 obligations of $1.4B. Carahsoft Technology’s mix of awards remains concentrated in Software Publishers and other IT services, which influences the overall obligation totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets matter most for Carahsoft Technology right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $695M to Carahsoft Technology in FY2026 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $233M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $115M. Software Publishers is the largest market at $1B, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $221M and an additional Software Publishers entry at $110M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Carahsoft Technology make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Carahsoft Technology has $1.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Carahsoft Technology’s FY2026 totals include 1,529 awards and an average award size of $941K. Carahsoft Technology’s obligations fell 20.5% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Carahsoft Technology?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense, Department of Health and Human Services, and Department of Homeland Security buy from Carahsoft Technology. The Department of Defense obligated $695M, the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $233M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $115M in FY2026 to date. Additional buyers include the Department of Agriculture at $99M and the Social Security Administration at $65.9M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Carahsoft Technology sell to the government?",
      "a": "Carahsoft Technology sells primarily software and IT services to the government. Software Publishers account for $1B and $110M in FY2026 to date, and Other Computer Related Services account for $221M. Carahsoft Technology also records awards in Custom Computer Programming Services at $64.4M and Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $21.8M."
    },
